# No dashes in site copy

Never use `—` (em dash), `–` (en dash), or `--` as punctuation or separators in user-facing text (UI strings, SEO metadata, heroes, FAQs, emails, admin labels).

## Use instead

- Comma, colon, period, or `|` depending on meaning
- Address / title separators: `,` or `|` (e.g. `India, 384440`, `Career | Nexuron Technologies`)
- Labeled lists: `Label: description` (not `Label — description`)
- Screen-reader hints: `: open full article` (not `— open`)

## Allowed

- Compound words / CSS / paths / flags: `full-stack`, `max-w-[1340px]`, `--fix`
- Numeric ranges with an en dash when idiomatic: `48–72 hours`, `2–4 months`
- Empty-state placeholders: a single `—` meaning “no value” in tables
- Code comments (not shown to visitors)

## Examples

```text
❌ trained on your business — available 24/7
✅ trained on your business. Available 24/7
✅ trained on your business: available 24/7

❌ Beyond the framework — this is what working with us looks like.
✅ Beyond the framework: this is what working with us looks like.

❌ India - 384440
✅ India, 384440
```
